 to eat you still got to live you've  still got to go on holiday how you going  to afford to do that so the goal is to  have enough passive income that covers  your life and that passive income can  pay the mortgage payments can pay the  car can pay your food can pay your  holiday financially free so generally  speaking before becoming debt free i'll  be coming financially free um however  most residential lenders are  usually want you to to to pay on a  repayment mortgage so i think either way  is okay the only exception is if you  love the house and you just feel like  you know what i just want to own this  outright one day nothing wrong with  repayment mortgages for buy to let's  generally interest only is better in my  opinion because you've got more cash  flow so it really is a personal decision  hope that helps david cook  i have nothing  but want to start my own company or  business is that possible says david  cook  well  it costs about 12 pounds to start a  company on company's house so if you  have nothing do you have 12 pounds  technically you can start a company for  12 pounds you can do it yourself on  companies house but the real definition  of a business is not just having a  limited company on companies house the  real definition of a business is having  something which is making money so can  you start with no money i would say  absolutely yes based on the fact that  i started all of my companies with no  money i never got a  business loan from a bank to start my  companies all of them have been my  letting agency my construction company  my buy to let company my training  company it was all started from nothing  the thing is this  if you want to make money through  business you have to find a way of  adding value so let's say you want to  get into property and you've got nothing  you literally and you don't even got the  12 pounds to set up a company the  question is  how can you  as a sole trader as just a person how  can you add value to people's lives how  can you help other people make money  maybe maybe you could go to estate  agents and start hustling and finding  cheap properties and then introduce  these cheap properties to investors and  guess what you're going to do if you do  that you're going to get paid  you're going to get paid to do that do  you have to have money to do that no  so i don't really think you need money  to start a business and there's millions  of successful businesses across the  planet that started with no money what  you need is you need creativity and you  need a good idea and you need a good  business plan so i hope that helps good  luck  music how can i find good deals in this  hot market what a great question i was  actually chatting with one of my friends  earlier and martin and mark was saying  to me that they just bought a property  and it was literally on the open market  they bought it for 215 000 pounds and i  said to them i asked them the same  question i said how did you buy it and  get it such a good deal  when the market's so hot it's in an open  market why did you not get out bit like  most people are complaining and they  said this this is really interesting  they said they didn't buy a property  that was going to be instantly a good  deal with a good return on investment  but they could see  that there was value to be added to the  property they're turning this property  into flats so it's one property they're  going to turn it into three flats  so  if you want to find good deals in this  marketplace right now while the market's  hard rather than trying to find  something that's going to give you an  instantly good return you need to be  finding opportunities that most people  can't see you need to be finding ways to  add value to properties that most people  might not be able to find for instance  find properties where there's there's um  a side plot you know or there's a garage  next to the house where you think  no one's noticed but i could potentially  get planning permission  to build another house next door  or find a property that's got a long  garden where potentially you could build  at the back of the garden or find a  property that is run down  and it's got strip it's got structural  problems and no one wants to touch it  but you know actually it's only going to  cost a few thousand pounds to get this  put right so rather than trying to find  good deals  you need to be good yourself you need to  become a good property problem solver be  able to find problems  where you can fix that problem and then  it becomes an opportunity when you get  good that's when you start finding good  deals jim rohn said don't wish it was  easier wish you were better and that's  so true in today's market when there's  so many people saying it's hard to find  a deal it's hard to find a deal so i  don't wish it was easier to find a deal  wish you were better at finding deals  wish you had more skills to spot the  opportunities so i think that's probably  what i would say because there's always  deals out there there's right now  there's loads of opportunities but you  need to be able to be trained well  enough to be able to spot those deals  hope that helps all right last question  don't forget folks i want to know your  questions so comment below this is from  alan partridge um allen said i wanted to  become a deal finder but it seems that  every man and his dog is one now surely  the market doesn't need tens of  thousands of deal finders surely it's  well over saturated now  that's a great question alan um i think  i'd probably say i'll answer that in a  few parts firstly there's lots of deal  finders out there yes but is there tens  of thousands of really good ones  i'm not sure there is i mean right now  you say every man on his dog is a deal  finder  i think right now every man in his dog  is desperately looking to get a good  deal but can't find one so that we're in  desperate need of good deal finders  another thing is as well 